# Landmark Extraction — Bug Diagnosis & Fix

## 🐛 Root Cause Found

The extraction was failing because of a **landmark count mismatch** between what MediaPipe actually produces and what the code expected:

### The Bug Chain

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["mediapipe_utils.py: refine_face_landmarks=True"] --> B["MediaPipe returns 478 face landmarks\n(468 mesh + 10 iris)"]
    C["mediapipe_utils.py: FACE = 468 * 3"] --> D["EXPECTED_SIZE = 1662"]
    B --> E["Actual extracted vector = 1692 dims"]
    D --> F["extract_landmarks.py checks:\nlandmarks.shape[0] == 1662"]
    E --> G["1692 ≠ 1662 → EVERY frame rejected"]
    F --> G
    G --> H["sequence is always empty → return None"]
    H --> I["'Skipping broken video' for ALL videos"]
```

| Component | Expected | Actual | Off by |
|-----------|----------|--------|--------|
| Face landmarks | 468 | **478** (iris refined) | +10 |
| Feature vector | 468×3 = 1404 | **478×3 = 1434** | +30 |
| Total size | 1662 | **1692** | +30 |

### Why 28 files existed in class 000
Those were from an **earlier version** of the script (before `EXPECTED_SIZE` validation was added). They have shape [(variable_frames, 1692)](file:///c:/Users/Bekal/Documents/my_own_documents/Uni_Diploma/Project/Model_training/KrSL_FluenSigners-50_Kuro/src/main.py#7-10) — no padding/truncation was applied.

---

## ✅ Fixes Applied

### 1. [mediapipe_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/Bekal/Documents/my_own_documents/Uni_Diploma/Project/Model_training/KrSL_FluenSigners-50_Kuro/src/utils/mediapipe_utils.py) — Fixed landmark count
```diff
-FACE = 468 * 3
+FACE = 478 * 3    # 478 because refine_face_landmarks=True adds 10 iris landmarks
```
`EXPECTED_SIZE` is now correctly **1692**.

### 2. [extract_landmarks.py](file:///c:/Users/Bekal/Documents/my_own_documents/Uni_Diploma/Project/Model_training/KrSL_FluenSigners-50_Kuro/src/preprocessing/extract_landmarks.py) — Rewritten for robustness

| Change | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| EXPECTED_SIZE | Duplicate hardcoded `1662` | Imported from `mediapipe_utils` |
| Dead code | `process_video()` unused | Removed |
| Error handling | Single exception → abort video | Per-frame try/except, continue |
| Target per class | Up to 100, no minimum | **MIN_VIDEOS_PER_CLASS = 15**, stops early when met |
| Long sequences | Hard truncation `[:30]` | **Uniform temporal sampling** (preserves full temporal coverage) |
| Short sequences | Zero-pad | Zero-pad (unchanged) |
| Reporting | Minimal prints | **Full summary** showing per-class success/failure counts |

---

## ⚠️ Old Data is Inconsistent

> [!WARNING]
> The 80+ existing keypoint folders contain data from a previous extraction run with **different shapes** (variable length, no padding). These will break training if mixed with new extractions.

**Recommended action:** Delete `data/keypoints/` contents and re-extract cleanly so all files have the uniform shape `(30, 1692)`.

---

## 📋 Next Steps

1. **Clear old keypoints**: Delete contents of `data/keypoints/`
2. **Re-run extraction**: `python -m src.preprocessing.extract_landmarks` (or run through PyCharm)
3. **Verify**: Each class should have 15+ `.npy` files, all with shape `(30, 1692)`
4. **Proceed to normalization/training**
